{{ end }}- Follow-up and dependency rules:
  - Atomic-merge test before reaching for `--deferred`: if the parent would land incorrect or incomplete in the base branch without this new piece, the new piece is part of the parent's merge unit. Track it as a normal child issue (child issues land in the same base-branch commit as the parent) or include it in the parent's commit — never `--deferred`. Reserve `--deferred` for work that can land separately later.
  - Create immediate child/blocking scope with `az issue create "Title"`; when `AZEDARACH_ISSUE_ID` is set this auto-creates a child issue under that parent.
  - Use `az issue create --deferred "Title"` only for standalone later/backlog work that should be tracked now but not executed before the active issue closes.
  - Do not use `--deferred` for child tasks, blockers, or work required before closing the active issue; create normal child issues instead.
  - When fanning out to subagents, split work until each child issue is independently actionable and fits within a single subagent context window.
  {{ if .OrchestrationViaNative }}- `orchestration.via` is `native`: orchestrate the split using native subagent/delegation commands in your AI harness, while keeping issue bookkeeping in `az issue`.
